<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 12.84 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 12.84 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annualised yield on an issue of Kazakhstan's three-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 12.84 percent at an auction on Tuesday from 13.10 percent at the last auction on July 1, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   July 8	     July 1</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K0910978     KZ43K0210973</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  400		  500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 1,517		2,057</p>
<p> Sold (nominal)			410		  507</p>
<p> Average price			 96.89 pct	  96.83</p>
<p> Average yield			 12.84 pct	  13.10</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Oct 9, 1997	Oct 2, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
<p>$=75.57 tenge</p>
</text>
